    "intro_html":  "Coq au vin is the French farmhouse braise that Julia Child taught America to make: chicken cooked slowly with bacon, mushrooms, onions, and carrots until the sauce turns dark and glossy and the meat gives up without a fight. This build braises in beef and chicken broth so it stays cheap and stays on the grocery board. If you happen to have red wine open, swap a cup of it in for some of the broth and you are back to the original. Each bowl runs 659 calories and \u003cstrong\u003e51 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$2.19 a serving\u003c/strong\u003e.",
